      "id": "claim_f2922c6881804267b4fea0755fce24be",
      "statement": "The server's single Shell owns a persistent Session whose virtual current directory, environment variables, and last status survive across tool calls; under stdio that state normally lasts for the client-owned server process, while a longer-lived HTTP server instance shares its one Shell across calls rather than creating per-client shells.",
