      "id": "claim_91299dc0e1b44cee8ac83a9731cc8555",
      "statement": "`run(command)` interprets commands in-process: `Shell.run` creates in-memory streams, parses and executes an AST, dispatches simple commands only through the Python builtin registry, and converts parse errors, loop limits, unknown commands, and builtin exceptions into shell statuses and terminal diagnostics rather than spawning host processes.",
